WEBVTT

00:35.890 --> 00:37.180
No...

00:37.180 --> 00:39.480
I do not wish to be alone again...

00:40.020 --> 00:42.830
However, it does not matter. I remember now.

00:42.830 --> 00:47.900
There is... That is right, 
there is someone who loves me.

00:48.420 --> 00:50.270
<i>What are you to me?!</i>

00:50.770 --> 00:53.860
No, what am I to you?!

01:09.170 --> 01:16.880
Spice and Wolf

02:28.330 --> 02:31.000
Goodness. What'd I tell you?

02:29.040 --> 02:33.040
<b>Episode 17
Traveling Merchant's Shallow Thinking and Town Merchant's Signboard</b>

02:31.420 --> 02:34.670
You were so confident. Look at yourself now.

02:34.670 --> 02:36.740
There was an unforeseen accident.

02:36.740 --> 02:38.260
It was completely unexpected and I—

02:38.260 --> 02:40.340
Just admit that you let your guard down.

02:41.110 --> 02:42.600
Be honest with yourself.

02:44.250 --> 02:45.510
You're absolutely right.

02:45.850 --> 02:48.030
So? What're you here for?

02:48.030 --> 02:50.740
If you're asking for money, 
I've got to turn you down.

02:50.740 --> 02:52.300
I want to know which way 
the wind is blowing.

02:52.690 --> 02:55.050
Even if I plan to set sail,

02:55.050 --> 03:00.110
as an outsider, it's hard to get 
a reading on the day-to-day market.

03:01.580 --> 03:02.910
Give it up.

03:03.630 --> 03:06.780
Just like how you can't stop 
a horse that's gained momentum,

03:06.780 --> 03:09.250
it's rare for rising prices to suddenly stop.

03:09.680 --> 03:12.790
The price board that was hastily made 
next to the stone merchant

03:12.790 --> 03:16.890
shows that the number of people waiting 
to buy keeps growing against the sellers.

03:17.730 --> 03:20.880
There's no hint of the price 
dropping within a day or two.

03:21.150 --> 03:25.510
Our almighty God is the only one 
who can change the direction of the wind.

03:26.280 --> 03:28.580
Then, I'll just have to pretend to be God.

03:30.030 --> 03:34.740
I can't imagine Amati falling 
for a predictable price drop.

03:35.630 --> 03:38.770
Are you trying to plan a price crash?

03:38.770 --> 03:40.230
What else can I do?

03:41.330 --> 03:48.420
I have to turn the pyrite in his hands 
into plain rocks by sunset tomorrow.

03:55.460 --> 03:58.170
A trap that'll make him 
misinterpret the market...

03:58.610 --> 04:00.810
Something that will cause
a crash in prices...

04:01.720 --> 04:03.590
Is there anything like that?

04:04.230 --> 04:06.700
Then, I'll just have to pretend to be God.

04:10.750 --> 04:11.810
God...

04:12.470 --> 04:15.940
Please tell me again at what price you 
wish to purchase these fur pelts? {Note: Ep3}

04:15.940 --> 04:21.190
It seems my vision 
has suddenly tilted one way... {Note: Ep7}

04:24.110 --> 04:25.200
Great sir. {Note: Ep10}

04:25.500 --> 04:27.830
Do you have the time to hesitate? {Note: Ep10}

04:28.520 --> 04:29.830
<i>If it were Holo...</i>

04:38.420 --> 04:40.230
Take a look at this!

04:40.750 --> 04:42.670
Don't be too surprised.

04:43.840 --> 04:45.720
Whoa...

04:45.720 --> 04:48.060
You went all in, didn't you?

04:48.060 --> 04:50.220
Are you planning on quitting 
your job as a wheat merchant?

04:50.480 --> 04:53.000
It's rumored that the price 
will be as much as double tomorrow.

04:53.000 --> 04:54.530
Double?! Are you sure?

04:54.530 --> 04:56.150
It's a solid bet.

04:56.150 --> 04:58.800
If you furled your sails 
just because of the festival,

04:58.800 --> 05:00.940
you'll miss the perfect 
chance to set sail!

05:00.940 --> 05:04.860
Looks like this isn't the time 
to be diligently buying wheat!

05:04.860 --> 05:06.520
You're right!

06:03.710 --> 06:04.800
That was delicious!

06:04.800 --> 06:07.230
The freshwater fish 
was just as good as rumored!

06:17.730 --> 06:18.790
Mr. Lawrence.

06:20.770 --> 06:22.900
Oh, excuse me.

06:22.900 --> 06:23.880
Can I help you?

06:23.880 --> 06:26.740
I have letters for you.

06:27.210 --> 06:28.240
Who are they from?

06:28.490 --> 06:31.100
They were both from your companion.

06:31.100 --> 06:34.700
One is written by me in place of 
your companion at her request.

06:36.150 --> 06:37.960
May I have a light?

06:40.370 --> 06:42.920
Two hundred silver coins in cash.

06:43.260 --> 06:47.060
Pyrite worth three hundred silver coins.

06:47.060 --> 06:48.920
Assets that can be liquidated...

06:49.320 --> 06:52.260
This is the division of Amati's assets!

06:56.680 --> 06:57.740
Holo...

07:01.850 --> 07:05.040
This is Amati's handwriting...

07:06.150 --> 07:07.400
Let's see.

07:07.400 --> 07:09.320
In God's name...

07:12.670 --> 07:14.910
Contract of marriage?!

07:20.070 --> 07:21.300
Holo...

07:26.000 --> 07:28.680
Please bring out all the money 
I've left with you!

07:33.910 --> 07:37.140
Bars that Mr. Amati regularly visits?

07:44.740 --> 07:46.330
What was that all about?

07:46.330 --> 07:48.030
It's that guy from the association!

07:53.050 --> 07:54.870
Hey! Watch where you're going!

08:03.050 --> 08:03.980
Excuse me.

08:10.250 --> 08:11.300
Good evening.

08:15.470 --> 08:16.750
Do you have business with me?

08:16.750 --> 08:18.830
There's no need to be so alarmed.

08:19.180 --> 08:21.390
I came to talk business with you.

08:26.040 --> 08:28.300
This is a nice and quiet place.

08:28.300 --> 08:30.940
It's difficult to enjoy 
a quiet drink in other places.

08:30.940 --> 08:32.740
This is a very valuable place of mine.

08:33.300 --> 08:36.040
What are you plotting?

08:36.040 --> 08:40.080
To be frank, 
I'd like you to buy my pyrite.

08:40.080 --> 08:40.680
Huh?

08:41.080 --> 08:43.420
I'd like you to buy my pyrite.

08:43.420 --> 08:46.170
I currently have five hundred Trenni 
silver coins worth of pyrite,

08:46.170 --> 08:48.000
according to today's market value.

08:48.000 --> 08:50.060
You must be joking.

08:50.060 --> 08:51.550
I'm not.

08:51.850 --> 08:55.950
You already know that I'm making money 
by reselling pyrite, don't you?

08:55.950 --> 09:00.330
Knowing that, what's your intention 
behind selling pyrite to me?!

09:00.330 --> 09:03.520
Could it be that you truly 
don't care about Ms. Holo

09:03.520 --> 09:06.140
as long as you recover the 
money owed to you?

09:06.140 --> 09:10.040
No, Holo is very precious to me.

09:10.040 --> 09:11.010
Why, then?

09:11.010 --> 09:14.150
Of course, I don't just 
plan to sell it to you.

09:14.750 --> 09:16.570
I'd like to sell it to you on credit.

09:16.570 --> 09:18.660
On credit?

09:18.660 --> 09:19.240
Yes.

09:19.240 --> 09:21.050
What do you mean?

09:21.050 --> 09:24.830
In other words, I'd like to sell you pyrite 
currently worth five hundred Trenni coins,

09:24.830 --> 09:27.940
at the current market value 
tomorrow evening.

09:27.940 --> 09:31.220
Then speak to me again tomorrow evening.

09:31.220 --> 09:33.960
No, I'd rather have 
the money right now.

09:35.470 --> 09:40.560
In other words, I'd like to receive 
five hundred coins, in advance, right now.

09:40.870 --> 09:48.770
Then, I will hand over the pyrite 
to you tomorrow evening.

09:52.380 --> 10:02.810
So, I'll get the pyrite calculated at today's
 rate even if the price has risen?

10:02.810 --> 10:03.830
That's right.

10:03.830 --> 10:07.950
For example, I sell you 
one piece of pyrite

10:07.950 --> 10:10.220
worth one thousand 
two hundred Illaid on credit.

10:10.220 --> 10:13.730
I would get the money from you now.

10:13.730 --> 10:17.490
Then, even if the pyrite is worth 
two thousand Illaid by the end of tomorrow,

10:17.490 --> 10:21.300
I would still give you 
that one piece of pyrite.

10:21.890 --> 10:26.140
On the other hand, even if the price 
drops down to two hundred Illaid,

10:26.140 --> 10:29.680
I will still only get one piece of pyrite.

10:29.680 --> 10:31.260
Exactly.

10:34.500 --> 10:37.070
Why not just trade normally?

10:37.360 --> 10:40.490
We're only putting a day 
between a standard trade.

10:40.490 --> 10:43.340
This is no different than usual...

10:44.650 --> 10:46.070
No, it <i>is</i> different.

10:47.430 --> 10:49.210
So, that's your plan.

10:49.660 --> 10:55.670
Selling on credit means receiving money 
by selling an item you don't have.

10:56.040 --> 10:59.620
If you buy on credit and the item 
gains that much in value,

10:59.620 --> 11:01.170
you make that amount of profit.

11:01.170 --> 11:04.550
So, if you <i>sell</i> on credit, you're 
hoping the value of money will increase.

11:05.810 --> 11:11.440
In other words, you want the value 
of the item you sell to decrease in value.

11:12.650 --> 11:15.640
As expected, 
you're quick to catch on.

11:15.640 --> 11:18.010
What an interesting way to do business.

11:18.010 --> 11:21.990
It looks like I cannot see the extent 
of this world if I only trade in fish.

11:21.990 --> 11:25.700
This time, you can gain a proportional 
profit from the rise in prices

11:25.700 --> 11:28.200
if you buy five hundred coins 
worth of pyrite from me,

11:28.200 --> 11:34.130
but your losses will be that much 
bigger if the value goes down.

11:34.130 --> 11:35.570
That's true.

11:35.570 --> 11:39.640
If you make a profit, I will take a loss.

11:39.640 --> 11:41.010
This is...

11:41.300 --> 11:44.970
Mr. Amati, I am challenging you to a duel.

11:49.540 --> 11:51.850
You can't really call this a duel.

11:52.140 --> 11:56.500
We can't possibly do this trade 
without putting it in writing.

11:56.500 --> 12:00.500
Even if the price goes down 
before the end of the day tomorrow,

12:00.500 --> 12:04.530
I will probably sell the loan 
document earlier in the day,

12:04.530 --> 12:06.990
as long as it rises enough to meet 
the amount needed for the contract.

12:06.990 --> 12:10.050
This is far too disadvantageous 
to you, Mr. Lawrence.

12:10.050 --> 12:15.790
After all, even a small rise in price 
would be enough for me to reach my goal.

12:15.790 --> 12:22.380
I don't wish to accept a deal 
where I gain from your loss.

12:22.950 --> 12:26.070
It may seem that way 
if you only look at this deal alone,

12:26.070 --> 12:29.380
but this amount of 
disadvantage is just right.

12:29.380 --> 12:30.310
What do you mean?

12:30.310 --> 12:34.980
There's a chance that Holo tears up 
the contract of marriage with you.

12:35.450 --> 12:37.770
You also have an agreement 
with her, don't you?

12:37.770 --> 12:40.860
Even if you pay off her 
one thousand silver coin debt,

12:40.860 --> 12:45.850
you're shouldering the heavy risk 
that she may not say yes.

12:45.850 --> 12:49.990
This disadvantage is minor 
compared to yours.

12:50.950 --> 12:54.410
I don't think that's something 
you need to worry about.

12:54.410 --> 12:57.130
I heard the two of you got 
into a very severe fight.

12:58.200 --> 13:02.210
Holo has cried in my arms three times 
since we started traveling together.

13:03.920 --> 13:09.420
She's pretty cute when she's like that, 
but she's a stubborn one.

13:10.300 --> 13:13.180
There are times when she acts 
in opposition to her feelings.

13:13.740 --> 13:14.590
In other words...

13:15.900 --> 13:17.370
I accept.

13:17.370 --> 13:19.690
I accept your challenge, Mr. Lawrence.

13:20.190 --> 13:22.660
I... I...

13:22.660 --> 13:29.000
I thought it would be too cruel of me 
to take everything away from you.

13:29.000 --> 13:32.950
However, if that's how you choose to speak, 
I accept this challenge.

13:33.640 --> 13:38.460
With it, I will take everything 
from you, Mr. Lawrence!

13:42.200 --> 13:44.340
Then, you accept this deal?

13:47.490 --> 13:49.010
Gladly!

13:56.740 --> 13:57.940
Cheers!

14:06.420 --> 14:07.570
This is good beer!

14:07.880 --> 14:10.900
Wheat harvests have been 
great everywhere this year.

14:10.900 --> 14:14.820
The wheat for beer has to be used for 
bread instead when the harvests are bad.

14:14.820 --> 14:17.000
Guess we have the gods 
of harvest to thank for that!

14:18.830 --> 14:20.040
You're right!

14:20.880 --> 14:25.310
But my business with you is a little 
too serious to be telling you over drinks...

14:25.870 --> 14:27.130
Is it a money-making scheme?

14:27.460 --> 14:29.140
I wonder about that...

14:29.140 --> 14:32.390
It's profitable in a sense, 
but that's not my goal this time.

14:32.680 --> 14:33.740
Meaning?

14:33.740 --> 14:37.570
Doesn't the wholesale purchase of wheat
 usually focus around the end of the festival?

14:37.570 --> 14:39.370
It does.

14:39.370 --> 14:42.230
I'd like a certain rumor to be spread.

14:42.570 --> 14:44.700
I'm not doing anything dangerous.

14:44.700 --> 14:46.860
It might be risky if <i>you</i> spread it yourself,

14:47.190 --> 14:50.660
but it shouldn't be a problem 
for your apprentice to say.

14:51.970 --> 14:53.050
Tell me what it is.

14:53.050 --> 14:56.290
When I give the signal, 
I want him to say this:

14:57.090 --> 15:00.000
"I wonder if it's about time 
for the price of wheat to go up."

15:02.660 --> 15:06.210
Are you planning to make the prices 
of those stones drop using a rumor?

15:06.460 --> 15:07.760
Something like that.

15:08.380 --> 15:10.780
Most of the people trading pyrite 
are traveling through

15:10.780 --> 15:15.140
to sell something and to buy 
something before heading back home.

15:15.140 --> 15:19.270
The item they're buying to 
take back is usually wheat.

15:20.080 --> 15:25.130
If the price of wheat is rumored to increase, 
they'll rush to buy it before that happens.

15:25.590 --> 15:29.930
They'll sell the pyrite they bought 
to earn some side money all at once.

15:30.350 --> 15:35.080
And that'll naturally 
lower the price of pyrite?

15:35.550 --> 15:39.960
I didn't think you'd be such a simpleton.

15:39.960 --> 15:41.330
That's not all.

15:41.330 --> 15:44.780
Once all that pyrite is on the market...

15:44.780 --> 15:45.840
How much?

15:46.190 --> 15:47.880
A thousand Trenni silver coins worth.

15:47.880 --> 15:48.890
A thousand?!

15:48.890 --> 15:52.700
Are you stupid?! Imagine 
how much that'll hurt your wallet!

15:52.700 --> 15:54.480
It doesn't matter how 
much the price drops.

15:55.150 --> 15:56.470
What the hell are you saying?!

15:56.720 --> 16:00.380
As long as I can get five hundred 
silver coins worth of pyrite,

16:00.380 --> 16:04.060
my wallet won't hurt 
whether the prices go up or down.

16:05.770 --> 16:08.110
Damn. You sold on credit.

16:08.110 --> 16:12.510
Yeah. I'm doing regular trading on credit,

16:12.510 --> 16:17.390
so my wallet is safe whether 
the price of pyrite goes up or down.

16:17.390 --> 16:19.230
In exchange, I get no gains, either.

16:20.870 --> 16:24.340
Amati might lose a lot 
of money or go bankrupt.

16:24.340 --> 16:26.750
Looks like you took 
advantage of his ignorance.

16:26.750 --> 16:29.250
No, I think he accepted 
the challenge fully knowing the risks.

16:29.250 --> 16:30.820
He said as much.

16:30.820 --> 16:35.240
Then, you still managed to get him 
to accept with that silver tongue of yours.

16:35.240 --> 16:36.590
You're such a scary guy.

16:36.590 --> 16:39.930
Is that all you wanted to ask me to do?

16:39.930 --> 16:41.230
There's one more thing.

16:41.230 --> 16:43.060
I want you to buy a large amount of pyrite.

16:43.530 --> 16:46.330
You didn't find a place to buy pyrite 
before signing the contract with him?!

16:46.330 --> 16:48.690
Unfortunately, 
I didn't have enough time.

16:48.690 --> 16:53.150
If I go around buying a lot of pyrite 
when the sun goes up,

16:53.150 --> 16:55.950
the prices will just continue to rise.

16:55.950 --> 16:59.440
I want to gather it secretly, 
without affecting the market.

16:59.870 --> 17:03.870
That's why I want you to use 
your connections as a town merchant.

17:04.890 --> 17:08.890
It's okay even if you buy it at a slightly 
higher price than the current market, in cash.

17:08.890 --> 17:12.260
I pay with Lumione gold coins 
once you've gathered enough.

17:12.260 --> 17:14.860
Of course, I'll pay you well 
for your efforts, too.

17:14.860 --> 17:15.720
I can't.

17:15.720 --> 17:18.140
I see. Then... What?

17:20.610 --> 17:22.850
I can't help you there.

17:22.850 --> 17:26.670
I'll pay you! I'm not talking 
about a small amount like wages.

17:26.670 --> 17:29.920
You've got nothing to lose! 
Isn't it a good deal?!

17:29.920 --> 17:31.150
I have nothing to lose?

17:31.150 --> 17:36.040
Of course! All I'm asking you 
to do is buy the pyrite!

17:36.040 --> 17:37.700
I'm not asking you to invest.

17:37.700 --> 17:39.870
And, of course, I'll pay you in cash.

17:39.870 --> 17:41.610
What would you lose 
in a situation like that?

17:42.230 --> 17:46.860
Lawrence, the max you can pay 
is about ten Lumione, right?

17:46.860 --> 17:48.500
Isn't that enough?!

17:48.810 --> 17:52.020
I'm not asking you to cross 
the steep mountains alone

17:52.020 --> 17:55.380
and bring back a crazy amount of pyrite.

17:55.380 --> 18:00.430
You're telling me to run around the market 
and gather the pyrite for you.

18:00.430 --> 18:01.580
That's practically the same.

18:01.580 --> 18:03.140
How is that—?!

18:07.990 --> 18:13.470
I just want you to use 
your connections to buy pyrite.

18:13.470 --> 18:16.460
I'm telling you that 
the danger's the same.

18:17.400 --> 18:20.700
The dangers you're talking about 
pertain to traveling merchants.

18:20.700 --> 18:24.950
But I'm a town merchant 
and my battlefield is this market.

18:24.950 --> 18:29.260
It's not virtuous for a town merchant 
to jump on any great money-making deal.

18:29.730 --> 18:33.050
Town merchants would rather make 
a modest living with their main job

18:33.050 --> 18:36.010
than make a large profit 
on a side venture.

18:37.050 --> 18:39.080
What will people think of me if I run around

18:39.080 --> 18:41.670
gathering five hundred 
silver coins worth of pyrite?

18:41.670 --> 18:43.130
They'll think of me as a hopeless man

18:43.130 --> 18:46.720
who drowned himself in gambling 
and abandoned his stall.

18:46.970 --> 18:51.230
I may be the owner of this stall, 
but I'm not the only one that's a part of it.

18:51.230 --> 18:53.610
All the people who have supported this place,

18:53.610 --> 18:57.820
my wife, children, and all of our relatives.

18:58.100 --> 19:00.950
The honor of all of those people 
is attached to this stall.

19:01.300 --> 19:04.740
Can you pay me enough money 
to match risking all of their honor?

19:05.330 --> 19:10.990
Even for a small shop like this, the price 
of my signboard is surprisingly expensive.

19:11.390 --> 19:16.670
If it gets damaged, a mere ten or twenty 
gold coins isn't enough to repair it.

19:21.140 --> 19:22.930
That's how things are.

19:25.070 --> 19:26.040
Sorry.

19:27.400 --> 19:30.190
No, I'm sorry for being unreasonable.

19:31.930 --> 19:34.940
Well, I'm sure you can't help it 
considering that companion of yours.

19:35.620 --> 19:39.100
You don't need to hinder 
him so desperately.

19:39.100 --> 19:41.980
She won't be swayed by 
him so easily, right?

19:42.490 --> 19:46.720
Even I thought so, after seeing her 
next to you for the first time.

19:47.230 --> 19:48.750
You should have more confidence!

19:49.140 --> 19:52.290
I was slapped with a contract 
of marriage with her signature on it.

19:52.290 --> 19:54.410
Of course, the other party is Amati.

19:54.830 --> 19:58.350
I'm not the type to 
lose confidence over nothing.

19:58.350 --> 20:00.350
But now, something has happened.

20:01.590 --> 20:03.990
In this world, darkness can always 
be found one step ahead of you.

20:04.420 --> 20:09.140
But you're still running around 
because you have a chance, right?

20:09.140 --> 20:11.720
So? You got any other angles to work with?

20:11.720 --> 20:14.880
I'll try talking to Mr. Batos first.

20:14.880 --> 20:15.860
I see.

20:15.860 --> 20:18.650
You plan on using that woman.

20:19.080 --> 20:20.090
That woman?

20:20.090 --> 20:21.680
Huh? Am I wrong?

20:21.680 --> 20:24.110
Didn't you meet that chronicler?

20:24.510 --> 20:27.840
I've met Ms. Diana, but I don't 
understand what you're talking about.

20:28.280 --> 20:32.860
I think it would be all right for an outsider 
like you to trade with that woman.

20:32.860 --> 20:34.370
I still don't get what you're talking about.

20:34.370 --> 20:37.800
That woman controls the northern district.

20:37.800 --> 20:41.550
She's the person to talk to 
if you want to deal with the alchemists.

20:41.860 --> 20:46.300
Alchemists are always targeted 
for various reasons.

20:46.600 --> 20:49.790
Everyone thinks the only reason so many 
can gather together is that woman.

20:49.790 --> 20:50.600
So, what?

20:50.600 --> 20:54.020
Alchemists have pyrite!

20:54.810 --> 21:00.760
They're the type of people that 
reputable businesses would never work with.

21:00.760 --> 21:01.960
In other words...

21:01.960 --> 21:04.530
No one has touched their pyrite!

21:04.810 --> 21:08.980
I'm happy you thought of depending on me, 
but this is all I can do for you.

21:08.980 --> 21:12.080
No, I almost missed a huge opportunity!

21:12.630 --> 21:16.130
I know I turned you down, 
but I'm really hoping for your success.

21:16.130 --> 21:19.290
I learned something. 
That alone is a huge windfall.

21:22.410 --> 21:24.720
I can't do things openly,

21:24.720 --> 21:28.380
but I can at least mutter about 
the financial situation of others.

21:29.080 --> 21:34.310
Come back later. I can at least point out 
places that might be interested in selling.

21:35.340 --> 21:36.350
That'll be a great help!

21:36.780 --> 21:42.510
To think you'd make a face like that. 
No wonder she's done something so bold.

21:42.510 --> 21:43.730
What do you mean?

21:43.730 --> 21:44.780
Nothing at all.

21:44.780 --> 21:48.450
I'm just saying that merchants 
should stick to thinking about business.

21:50.360 --> 21:52.450
I'm sure a good wind will blow.

21:52.830 --> 21:54.080
Well, try your best!

21:57.530 --> 21:58.460
See you later!

